Front-classify ZRANGEBYSCORE's LIMIT form (frankenredis-50ntn / ayiy7)

WHY THIS IS A PATCH FILE AND NOT AN EDIT. /data has sat at 58.1-58.4G against a 59G
floor for three turns, so there is no build slot and I cannot compile this. An
uncompiled edit to crates/fr-server/src/main.rs reddens every pane's suite during a
disk crisis, and an uncommitted edit does not stay parked -- last time one was swept
into a peer's commit stripped of its caveats (frankenredis-fhgvc). A committed patch
has the review value of real code and none of the blast radius.

APPLY WITH:
    git apply scripts/zrangebyscore_limit_classify.patch
then, before trusting it:
    python3 scripts/build_preflight.py          # must print CLEAR TO BUILD
    cargo build --release -p fr-server --bin frankenredis --features perf-ab-cascade-bypass
    strings <binary> | grep -c FR_PERF_AB_CASCADE_BYPASS    # must be 1, not 0
    <three-way differ; the 14 ZRANGEBYSCORE rows are already in the corpus at 8bd375ac6>

WHY IT IS SAFE TO CLAIM ARITY 7 WITHOUT A KEYWORD CHECK. Every ZRANGEBYSCORE array
length carries exactly one form -- 4 plain, 5 WITHSCORES, 7 LIMIT, 8 WITHSCORES LIMIT
(scripts/arity_misclaim_screen.py --advise ZRANGEBYSCORE). This is NOT ZRANGE, where
arity 5 carries four rival forms and the discrimination had to live in the arm
(frankenredis-jnf09). The arm below still tests the LIMIT token, because the classifier
promises only a LENGTH and the token is what the parser was given.

THE ARM IS A COPY OF THE CASCADE ARM AT main.rs:12375, with `out` in place of
`&mut conn.write_buf`, which is the same transposition every other floor arm makes.
The executor it calls -- execute_plain_zrangebyscore_limit_borrowed_into -- is the
zero-copy `_into` member-borrow path and already exists; nothing new is written.

